# AI Detector — Integration Plan for HiveLogic

## Overview

Add an `AIDetector` class to the agent-side detection pipeline that calls an external LLM API (Ollama) to analyze log batches for anomalous patterns that regex-based rules miss. It plugs into the existing detector framework alongside `SlidingWindowDetector` and `CorrelationDetector`.

## Files to Create/Modify

### New Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `hivelogic/ai_detector.py` | `AIDetector` class + Ollama API client |
| `AI/ai_detector.plan` | This plan document |

### Modified Files

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `hivelogic/detectors.py` | Add `AIDetection` dataclass |
| `hivelogic/log_processor.py` | Wire `AIDetector` into `_on_line()` pipeline |
| `hivelogic/daemon.py` | Handle `AIDetection` in `_on_detection()` |
| `hivelogic/config.py` | Add `ai_detector` config section |
| `config/config.example.yaml` | Document new config options |

